    {
      "block_id": "2605.28896_p13_b14",
      "text": "The convergence of three different measures reduces the risk of any single metric being misleading.\nCosine similarity could in principle reflect SAE training variance; principal angles address this\nby operating directly on the full decoder matrices without SAE decomposition; CKA validates\nat the activation level rather than the weight level.\n",
      "bbox": [
